&lt;p&gt; Medicare covers these tests when they are reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of  the following conditions:&lt;&sol;p&gt;  

&lt;ul&gt;   
&lt;li&gt; Genetic disorders (e.g., mongolism) in a fetus; (See the Medicare Benefit Policy Chapter 15, &quot;Covered Medical and Other Health Services,&quot; &amp;#167;20.1)&lt;&sol;li&gt;  

&lt;li&gt; Failure of sexual development;&lt;&sol;li&gt;  

&lt;li&gt; Chronic myelogenous leukemia;&lt;&sol;li&gt;  

&lt;li&gt; Acute leukemias lymphoid (FAB L1-L3), myeloid (FAB M0-M7), and unclassified; or&lt;&sol;li&gt;  

&lt;li&gt; Mylodysplasia&lt;&sol;li&gt;  
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

